WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.770
Sometimes you need a little help.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:07.858
In this video you will see where help lives in
OurWater, how to send feedback,

00:00:07.978 --> 00:00:11.650
where to learn about water, and who is behind
the app.

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:17.235
All the help pages live in the Account group,
near the bottom of the left menu.

00:00:17.355 --> 00:00:19.227
Click Account to open it.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:26.242
The last three links are for this video: Support,
About OurWater, and Learn about water.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.362
Support is the first place to look when you
are stuck.

00:00:30.482 --> 00:00:32.354
It has five cards.

00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:36.999
Send feedback opens a short form inside
OurWater.

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:40.311
Use it to report a problem or share an idea.

00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:45.677
Email us opens your mail app, ready to write
to the OurWater team.

00:00:45.797 --> 00:00:48.677
They reply within a few business days.

00:00:49.483 --> 00:00:52.051
The Phone card is grey on purpose.

00:00:52.171 --> 00:00:56.083
There is no support number yet, so tapping it
does nothing.

00:00:56.917 --> 00:01:03.013
Terms and Conditions explains what you agree
to, including how shared data may be reused.

00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:09.241
The Privacy Policy explains what personal
information is kept, and who can see it.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.186
This is the feedback form.

00:01:12.306 --> 00:01:14.658
See the Send feedback button?

00:01:14.778 --> 00:01:18.378
It looks faded until you add a star or some
words.

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:21.895
First, say what this is about.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:30.007
There are six choices: broken, confusing, an idea, a
data problem, report content, or something else.

00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:32.761
Tap the one that fits.

00:01:32.881 --> 00:01:36.841
Here we pick I have an idea, and the button
turns solid.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.762
Next, the stars.

00:01:39.882 --> 00:01:44.130
Tap one to say how OurWater is working, from
one to five.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.218
This part is optional.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.826
In Tell us more, write in your own words what
happened and what you hoped for.

00:01:51.946 --> 00:01:54.226
Short and simple is fine.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:01.122
Tap What is sent with this to see what travels
with your message: the app, version, device,

00:02:01.242 --> 00:02:03.210
screen and connection.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.202
Nothing else.

00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:08.321
Now Send feedback is ready.

00:02:08.441 --> 00:02:11.057
Tap it and the team reads your message.

00:02:11.177 --> 00:02:14.033
We stop here, so nothing is sent.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:19.746
After a few saved measurements, OurWater may
ask this one-tap question.

00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:24.282
Tap a star to answer, or choose Not now or
Don't ask again.

00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:29.163
To ask the people who run your own group, open
Messages.

00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:33.003
The Message admin button writes straight to an
administrator.

00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:38.929
Choose who gets it, write a subject and your
question, then tap Send to admin.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:41.137
They can see who it is from.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:48.382
Learn about water starts with Using OurWater: cards
that jump to adding a station, adding a measurement,

00:02:48.502 --> 00:02:50.374
and the map.

00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:54.399
Then come three cards about the water itself.

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:59.271
Each opens a short explanation on the MARVI
website, in a new tab.

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:03.899
About OurWater tells you who made the app, and
why.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:06.899
It is a free app for watching water together.

00:03:07.717 --> 00:03:13.357
The link, Learn more about MARVI, opens the
project's own website in a new tab.

00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:19.943
Key features lists what you can do: add
stations, record measurements, see a map,

00:03:20.063 --> 00:03:23.951
compare past and present, and use many
languages.

00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:27.855
Making water visible makes two promises.

00:03:27.975 --> 00:03:33.927
OurWater stays free, and shared measurements may be
shown publicly for learning and research.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.646
The yellow note matters.

00:03:36.766 --> 00:03:42.838
Use OurWater to learn, not as the only basis
for decisions about drinking water or health.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:48.786
Acknowledgements thank the funders, ACIAR and
the Australian Water Partnership,

00:03:48.906 --> 00:03:51.762
and the seven partner organisations.

00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:55.895
A special thank you goes to the Bhujal
Jaankaars,

00:03:56.015 --> 00:03:59.663
and the farmers and villages whose monitoring
shaped this app.

00:04:00.483 --> 00:04:05.115
At the bottom, Supported by names the funders
and partners once more.

00:04:05.235 --> 00:04:07.131
That is the whole tour.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:15.558
You can find all the OurWater tutorials on our website, at
ourwater.org.au, in the Tutorials section.

00:04:15.678 --> 00:04:18.126
That address is on the screen now.

00:04:18.246 --> 00:04:21.126
Thank you for helping look after our water.
